entityDescription:
For many years we have remained a manufacturer and comprehensive supplier of modern passenger information and related systems.
Our goal is to create and implement solutions that will ensure the highest quality of passenger service, full integrability, online monitoring, and simplicity in passenger traffic management by railway, while providing all the required functions.
SAT-System is a full-service provider, not just of the hardweare solutions themselves, but of complete software platforms, enabling integration with the national railway servers. Our devices and software can display information and make messages in any language. The language barrier for us does not exist. Functionally, we are able to create a complete system with devices for any market, according to the requirements of a given rail infrastructure operator.
We currently offer systems:
- complete dynamic passenger information system &ndash; HUSAR SIP &ndash; including all necessary station and platform equipment, including train movement sensors;
- public address system &ndash; HUSAR SR &ndash; enabling real-time and automatic announcements to be made from the railroad server, as well as locally from the station or local dispatcher center;
- paging and alarm system &ndash; HUSAR SPA &ndash; communication and intercom system providing full two-way audio video communication along with a system for the deaf or hard of hearing;
- integration platform &ndash; FALCON PSIM &ndash; enables efficient management of both dedicated railroad systems produced by SAT &ndash; SYSTEM and external security systems located at the station and platforms.
In addition to complete systems, we also offer individual manufactured solutions:
- full-range displays (main station; collective station; edge; platform; tunnel);
- multi-functional standing and pendant operating displays (single-sided and double-sided ; also with integrated clocks);
- clocks (indoor; outdoor; tower; single-sided and double-sided);
- public address system components (DSP amplifiers; loudspeakers; microphone units; ANS sensors);
- SOS alarm devices (standing, surface-mounted pendants; in wall-mounted panels; operator panels);
- intercoms and call systems (standing; wall-mounted; recessed; counter-window; with induction loop; for rest rooms);
- train movement sensors;
- automatic warning system for approaching trains.
All elements of the passenger information system were designed to meet the latest standards of the Polish State Railways. The list of railroad stations, where our systems are in operation or are currently being built, is approaching the round number of 100.

